        detailedDescription: "The Bas\xEDlica de la Sagrada Fam\xEDlia, also known as the Sagrada Fam\xEDlia, is a large unfinished Roman Catholic minor basilica in Barcelona, Catalonia, Spain. Designed by Catalan architect Antoni Gaud\xED (1852\u20131926), his work on the building is part of a UNESCO World Heritage Site. Construction began in 1882 and is projected to be completed in 2026, the centenary of Gaud\xED's death. Combining Gothic and Art Nouveau forms, the Sagrada Fam\xEDlia is renowned for its unique architectural style featuring organic shapes inspired by nature. The basilica has three grand facades: the Nativity facade, the Passion facade, and the Glory facade, each telling a different part of the story of Jesus. The interior is equally spectacular, with towering columns designed to resemble trees in a forest, creating a stunning canopy effect.",
        historicalInfo: "Construction of the Sagrada Fam\xEDlia started in 1882 under architect Francisco de Paula del Villar. In 1883, Antoni Gaud\xED took over the project and transformed it with his architectural vision. He worked on the church for 43 years until his death in 1926. Gaud\xED devoted his final years exclusively to the project, and at the time of his death, less than a quarter of the project was complete.",
