    category: "Park",
    detailedDescription: `Park G\xFCell is a public park system composed of gardens and architectural elements located on Carmel Hill in Barcelona, Catalonia, Spain. Designed by Antoni Gaud\xED and built between 1900 and 1914, the park was originally developed as a housing site by Eusebi G\xFCell. It was officially opened as a public park in 1926. The park showcases Gaud\xED's unique architectural and artistic style with colorful ceramic mosaics, undulating forms, and organic shapes inspired by nature. The famous serpentine bench covered in trencad\xEDs (broken ceramic tiles) offers panoramic views of Barcelona and the Mediterranean Sea. The park includes the famous dragon/lizard sculpture known as "El Drac" covered in colorful mosaic, which has become a symbol of Barcelona.`,
